The Congress agrees with the MIFID directive, which came into force on 1 November.
In parallel to the parliamentary elaboration, which ended its session today with the congressional decision in the Senate on the supplementary/amending requests for amendments belonging to the project, the government released the provisions resulting from the new law, with the intention of enabling the entry into force of both regulations by the end of the year.
The representatives of the various companies unanimously praised the efforts of congressmen and Senate deputies who, in their negotiations and votes, had aimed to establish the best possible regulation, which ensures the safety of investors and regulates the individual entrepreneurial activities, in order to guarantee a generally efficient market event.
MIFID, which redefines the Investment Services Regulations, pursues, in addition to the modernisation of the financial markets, an improvement in investor protection, an increase in the control claim of the Spanish Securities Commission (CNMV) and the promotion of cooperation between the various control authorities of the European Union.
The new directive makes it possible to offer financial advice to both specialised firms as well as natural or legal persons and also contributes to the establishment of new financial services (ESIS), the consultancies that merge with the investment and brokerage companies of securities.
In addition, it expands the number of systems for the execution of financial transactions so that the regulated circulating markets will be added the multilateral systems of the securities business and the systems for the internationalisation of trade orders, which would eventually compete with the current economic actors.
The law obliges the investment companies to announce the priorities of their company profile, the confrontation and the forms of dealing with risks in the market and to register all projects carried out in order to make it easier for the CNMV to carry out their control task.
The Economic Commission of the Congress provided for further changes in retrospect, whereby the decision that the titled bond must noward must now be regarded as “complex” funding for the investor due to its high level of risk has been confirmed by the U.S. mortgage and banking crisis. (U.S. mortgage crisis)
In addition, the entry into force of the directive on the legal confinement of the fields of qualified economists was used; 30 years after that the regulation, which restricted the working areas reserved for economists, was adopted 30 years after which the ordinance which restricted the areas reserved for economists.
The Senate, for its part, set new positions in the financial sector, such as that of the economic mediator, which works on foreign accounts, does not require authorization on the part of CNMV and can offer its services to commercialize products and at the same time customer acquisition of several investment companies.
The harmonised index of consumer prices (CPI) rose by five-tenths in November and now stands at 4.1%.
The indicator used by Eurostat to assess the rate of inflaturation within the European Union provides the average price trends that took place in Spain in November.
Its publication complies with the principles of Eurostat and the European Central Bank (ECB), which, by announcing the data, seeks a comparison of location and quality towards U.S. products.
The forecast for the indicator can be prepared prematurely by adopting the same approach as the harmonised consumer price index, but at the same time using various other statistical modelling methods to assess the information not available at the time of the calculation.
However, the Spanish Statistical Office (INE) warned that the previously determined indicator would only serve as an indicative value and would therefore not have to agree with the definitive result, which will be announced next 14 December.
“The Consumer Price Index (VPI) will continue to be at a relatively high level”
According to Deputy Prime Minister and Economy Minister Pedro Solbes, the rise of the CPI in November is a “temporary development”; at the same time, he assured that the price index would remain at a “relatively high” level in the coming months.
Nevertheless, Solbes noted in the halls of the congress building that “even if the current figure is not good”, Spain’s difference in inflation with the other members of the monetary union in recent years has remained “more or less”.
In addition, he explained that there were “fewer surprises” in November than in the previous month, during which the government did not expect such a high increase.
"We expected a value of around 4%", the Minister for Economic Affairs and Finance announced with regard to the forecast published today.
Virgin calculates revenues of over 42 billion euros over the next three years
Northern Rock's inventories have fallen by more than half, after the bank asked the British central bank for an emergency loan in mid-September of last year due to the crisis, and they are now only 12,000 million pounds (equivalent to 16,800 million euros).
At that time, the bank's assets amounted to a record-breaking 25,000 million pounds, a sum that fell considerably within two-and-a-half months due to customers' loss of confidence, and even despite the government's one-on-on-on-one guarantee that the money would be safe, will continue to fall by the end of the crisis.
The company Virgin, which would continue the group after the takeover under the brand name Virgin Money, must contribute about a quarter of the income of the British banks, which will be made up there from the investments of the next three years, in order to acquire exactly those 18 billion pounds, which are still needed to achieve its target of 30 billion.
Multimillionair Richard Branson's multi-millionaire, known through his eye-catching advertising campaigns in the UK, intends to invest 50,000 million pounds (equivalent to about 70 million euros) annually in advertising and marketing campaigns in order to achieve its goal.
Northern Rock this week named the Virgin Group, in which three other companies are involved, as its preferred bidder to lead it out of bankruptcy.
The mayor of Totana arrested on alleged suspicion of participation in urban corruption
The Spanish police arrested the current mayor of Totano (Partido Popular) belonging to the municipality of Murcia this morning due to the urgent suspicion of involvement in urban corruption, which was uncovered this week.
In addition, one of the secretaries of the municipal council and the head of the municipal police were arrested.
José Martínez Andreo represented the office of Juan Morales, currently deputy of the Partido Popular and then chairman of the municipal council of Totana at the time, and, according to information from the radio station Cadena SER, could be the original mastermind of the plot.
Officials will continue to search the business records of the municipality and the Ministry of Urban Planning and will not rule out further arrests in the coming hours.
In addition, Juan Morales's lawyer, the prime suspect was accused in the case of urban corruption discovered earlier this week.
According to information from the Cadena SER, the "popular" lawyer was arrested, and consequently privileged deputy Juan Morales was arrested on leaving his client's residence due to important incriminating documents that are said to be related to the plot.
In addition, other sources of information report the supposed order payments Morales to a Galician construction company, which provided for the conclusion of an urban development contract, in which the development of a 200-hectare area was decided.
Eight people are currently in custody.
Bono agrees to accept the candidacy of the PSOE in Toledo and, falling an electoral victory, in Congress.
Former Defense Minister José Bono has accepted the offer by the president and secretary-general of the Socialists, José Luis Rodriguez Zapatero. Accordingly, he will lead the list of PSOE candidates in the upcoming general elections in Toledo and, in the event of an election victory by the Socialists, take over the office of the President of Congress.
This is how José Blanco, organizing secretary of the PSOE, and Bono announced it in the press conference after a meeting with Zapatero took place today at the party's headquarters.
According to the head of government, the offer to the former minister is justified, since it is “important in politics to be able to count on the best” and Bono “is among the best.”
In addition, in the event of a victory for the Socialists in the coming elections, the politician, who comes from Mancha, would “apparently appear” to be the chairman of the congress for the party.
Bono would replace Manuel Martín as congressional president. He had announced last 15 November that he would no longever compete in the next general elections to end his career in public policy and instead campaign for climate protection in the university area.
The former minister had to admit that since his resignation two years ago, the presidential president had continuously pushed for his return to political events.
Moreover, he pointed out that, as with the appointment of the Vice-President for Economic Affairs, the party does not want to deprive the citizens of who would take over the post of President of Congress in the event of an election victory and described this as an "act of transparency".
If he actually takes office, he hopes to transform the chamber into a “house of respect and not insulting or shouting”, in order to make it seem more and more similar to citizens.”
“Regrettably, from time to time you get the impression that the only place where you can’t talk quietly and calmly in Madrid is the Congress; so the government president in the Senate was interrupted up to 26 times.”
At the same time, he praised the current President Manuel Martín and "his good work" and hinted that he did not want to appear to have already taken over the office, otherwise his political opponents would describe this as "arrogance".
Climate propaganda
Since the climate debate puts both the skeptics of climate change and those who put a social and political debate at the forefront in the foreground, the movement as a whole must show strong cohesion.
Especially if it is a leader of the movement who, as in the case of President Zapatero, considers the fight against climate change to be more important than the fight against Islamic terrorism and even proposes to conclude a “new treaty with the planet.”
However, this proposal puts him in need of explanation with regard to his government’s actions or non-actions, which has made a decisive contribution to Spain being at the forefront within the EU of the countries that have least met the requirements of the Kioto Protocol.
Who are those responsible for not meeting the targets, to which sectors this is due, and why did his government, which had proposed the “contract with the planet”, not stopped this development.
In addition, he is now forced to present to the Spanish citizens the measures he envisaged against climate change without further ado.
Which companies will be affected by this, which behavior of the citizens should be changed, which individual and collective austerity measures have to be carried out and what economic consequences result from it.
More specifically, who has to sacrifice himself and will pay to save the planet.
However, it has and will not have any such explanations in the future.
Precisely because it's about sacrificing and paying.
Because the measures, which can be used in real terms against climate change, are unpopular.
They are inexpensive, inconvenient and threatening to the accounts of the companies and citizens.
Even Zapatero, proposed by the PSOE, seemed so dangerous from an electoral strategic point of view that he was forced to withdraw the proposal again.
Accordingly, it is now necessary to save the planet with nothingness, i.e. with pure propaganda and empty sayings without any real consequences.
With impressive statements, commissions, committees, protocols and new offices.
With his contracts with the planet, the politician otherwise suitable for election campaigns does not have to talk or accuse, nor demand, but instead pursues the demanding issue of decorating the meetings and delighting others with his gentleness and kindness.
However, this can only happen if the contract does not deviate from its purely virtual nature and therefore does not pretend that the bicycle will become the only means of transport in the future or if we are only allowed to refresh ourselves with one fan.
The mayor and Totana's police chief due to an alleged involvement in urban corruption.
The Guardia Civil has arrested the mayor of Murcia's village of Totana, the "popular" politician José Martínez Andreo. In addition, the local police chief, the secretary of the mayor's office and a hotel entrepreneur have been taken into custody because of the alleged suspicion of urban planning violations, it was said today from investigative circles.
The city council was arrested at its residence, from where it was taken to the municipal office and in the premises of which it is located up to now, surrounded by numerous agents, who had also arrived at the municipal administration and with the municipal construction management Suelo Industrial y Vivienda.
The three arrests are related to the manhunts that had already taken place last Monday in Galicia, Murcia and Madrid, in which it turned out that more than 2 million hectares of untapped building land for urban development projects under the direction of the Galician construction company Nuaria were to be redesigned.
In addition, two other people were not directly arrested, but subjected to an investigation, which is initiated and carried out by the first court of Totona.
The first six arrestees were brought before the judge today.
According to investigative circles, the former mayor of Totana and current independent PP deputy Juan Morales is also being investigated.
Furthermore, his ex-wife, owner of a real estate company registered in Totana, as well as his current girlfriend residing in Murcia are under suspicion.
The chairman and owner of the group Nuaria, Vigo-born lawyer and entrepreneur Manuel N.A., was arrested in the village of Nigrán (Pontevedra), as well as the managing director of Suelo de Inmonuar Pablo José M.G., whose company acts as a sub-group of Nuaria and is said to have received the bribe.
The investigation is carried out by the municipal authority against urban planning offences, under the supervision of the central unit of Guardia Civil, whose representatives carried out eleven further searches in addition to the arrests, most of them in companies that were directly related to the arrests that took place in Madrid, Vigo, Murcia, Pontevedra, Las Rozas (Madrid) and Totana.
At that time, only a single person was arrested in Totana: the holder of a regionally known poultry farmer, who is said to have acted as a middleman.
Nuaria has been commissioned to build the largest residential complex of Murcia, which includes more than 5000 apartments, a golf course and two spa hotels.
The company acquired over 2.2 million square kilometers of space in Totana, which had to be reconstructed. The aim was to realize a construction project, which would raise the population of the municipality to 25,000 inhabitants.
The Nuaria Group includes other companies such as Autesa and Inomonuar, which promote the sale of real estate; Conyase, which in Vigo operates the parking lots of the streets Coruña, Venezuela and those of Plaza Fernando el Católico; Hogartel, whose activity is limited to the sector of direct marketing and Preconiza, specializing in the promotion, sales and installation of components.
