Our Finnish correspondent explains to us the commentary published yesterday in the most important Finnish newspaper, Helsingin Sanomat (Finland, by the way, is at the head of the PISA study), which comments on the note published in the same newspaper on 18 November; coincidentally on that date, the issue of which included the criticism of the book of Blackburn.
The content of philosophy has become the topic of public debate after the tragedy surrounding Jokela's school.
Responsible for the gruesome murders is a high school graduate who, in his news, cited Plato's and Nietzsche's works.
In an interview with the newspaper Helsingin Sanomat, the Chairman of the Educational Council for Philosophy, Pekka Elo, called on the teachers to take a more critical position vis-à-vis Plato and proposed to remove Plato’s teaching from the lower-level curricula for the subject of philosophy at grammar schools.
